                                     declared as a Prerequisite below]
```

## Prerequisites

**1. `src/service/parseBrainAide/`** must export the marker-pair
grammar with the renamed `playbook` / `research` fields. Already
satisfied (24/24 in its plan, 61/61 tests green per the breakage
report). The contract this plan consumes:

- `parseBrainAideFromString(content)` returns
  `{ kind: "ok", config, prose, playbook, research }` when the
  content carries exactly the three required marker pairs in
  fixed order.
- `parseBrainAide(root)` reads `.aide/config/brain.aide` and
  delegates to the same string parser.
- `interpolateArgs(config)` substitutes `${...}` placeholders in
  `mcpServerConfig.args` against frontmatter fields (no-op on the
  default scaffold).

**2. `src/service/install/provisionBrain/obsidianBrainAideTemplate/`**
must emit a default brain.aide whose body carries the three required
marker pairs in fixed order. Governed by Plan 1 in this cascade
(see sibling `obsidianBrainAideTemplate/plan.aide`). The contract
this plan consumes:

- `obsidianBrainAideTemplate(rootPath: string): string` returns a
  string that round-trips through `parseBrainAideFromString` to
  `kind: "ok"` with `result.playbook` and `result.research`
  carrying the playbook and research entry-point artifact bytes.
- The emitted prose body uses storage-agnostic vocabulary (no
  `vault`, no `wikilink`, no `hub` standalone) but preserves the
  MCP tool-name sentinels (`mcp__brain__read_note`,
  `mcp__brain__search_notes`) and the entry-point file paths
  (`coding-playbook/coding-playbook.md`,
  `research/research.md`) that this module's tests assert on.

If Plan 1 has not landed when this plan executes, every cold-install
test that derives entry-point bytes from the template will fail —
the template's body still carries the retired heading grammar and
parses as `malformed-body`. Run Plan 1 first.

